From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: a 4-address STA-MLD with two links is MLO capable

941 gave the 4-address WDS child its identity back, but the per-link
breakdown it was written for still never reaches ubus: every such child
is published with mlo_capable false, and wifimngr gates the whole
mlo_links array on that flag, so the array is simply absent.

Measured 2026-08-07 on the running mesh. Both backhaul children of the
controller hold two links:

  Link 0  BSSID 86:f7:56:41:01:d4  freq 5180.0
  Link 1  BSSID 76:04:1c:81:bc:2f  freq 6135.0

while ubus call wifi.apmld.ap-mld-2 stations reports, for both:

  "mlo_capable": false,
  "link_id": 0,

and no mlo_links at all.

The cause is inside iface_get_mlsta_4addr_info(). It counts the links
correctly, but the only place it can set mlo_capable is a test that the
MLD address differs from the station address - and a few lines earlier
the same function fills both from the address the caller asked about, so
on mt76 they always compare equal. That test is kept, because a driver
which does report a distinct MLD address still benefits from it; what
was missing is the plain criterion the non-4addr path a few lines below
already applies: more than one link is what makes a station MLO.

Why 941 was reported as verified on hardware: its check was "real MAC
and BSSID, real stats, link ids present", and every part of that was
true then and is true now. The per-link breakdown - the thing the patch
existed for - was not the thing looked at.

Verify on hardware, on the goal rather than on what is easy to see:
ubus call wifi.apmld.<backhaul-mld> stations on a node with a 4-address
child must report mlo_capable true and an mlo_links array holding one
entry per link the child actually has; iw dev <bsta> link on the child
says how many that should be.

--- a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
@@ -1951,6 +1951,16 @@
 		mlsta->num_link++;
 	}
 
+	/* Mirror iface_get_mlsta_info() below: more than one link is what makes
+	 * a station MLO. The per-link test above cannot fire on mt76, because
+	 * this path fills macaddr and mld_macaddr from the same address the
+	 * caller asked about, so they always compare equal - which left every
+	 * 4-address child published with mlo_capable false, and wifimngr gates
+	 * the whole per-link breakdown on that flag, so no mlo_links came out
+	 * at all (measured 2026-08-07: two links on the air, none reported). */
+	if (mlsta->num_link > 1)
+		mlsta->mlo_capable = 1;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
